    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0348" n="1026" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1026"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Kreismann</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 13, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of August 22 (No. 12) has
                    been received. The leading features of the project of reform, as laid before the
                    congress of German princes which lately assembled at Frankfort, by the Emperor
                    of Austria, are stated by you with great clearness, and your reflections upon
                    the subject, as well as upon other questions which at present engage the
                    attention of the German states, are interesting and instructive.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hermann Kreismann</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Berlin.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
